  "display_title": "Redemption",
  "description": "In 1866, during a time of Catholic persecution in Hwayeonguk, a boy named Mum-Yeong lives abandoned and downtrodden. Born to a *Baek-Jeong*—an untouchable social caste forced to work as butchers and regarded as less than human—he does whatever it takes to survive, earning the cruel nickname \"Dog Bastard.\" One day, Eun-Hak, a Catholic scholar, enters his life, and Mum-Yeong's slaughterhouse becomes a secret place of worship. \n\nA boy who wanted only to live, no matter how defiled or broken he became… A cruel and sorrowful love blossoms on the border between salvation and ruin. \n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)",
